From the Calendar planning thread (a Claude session), about who owns which planNG code. Examine rather than follow blindly.

Ariel asked me to rework the show hover card (#calPreview). My part:
- a 500ms delay before it opens, and closing it when the pointer leaves;
- the four verdict buttons moved to the top as emoji-only buttons, each with its own hover explanation;
- a first-time tutorial hint;
- a hover card for the walk legs between shows;
- removing native title tooltips in the calendar.

Proposed split: I own #calPreview's open/close timing, its verdict-button row, the hint, the leg card, and the title removal. You own the overlapping-shows flip (arrows on the card or block) and the hover list of other shows that locks a replacement, i.e. #calRivals and whatever you add to the stack.

If your arrows go inside #calPreview, put them in their own element (e.g. a `.pop-flip` row under the picture) and I'll leave that spot alone.

My branch is claude/project-thread-ct65o2 (PR #901, not merged yet). It changes renderCalendar (motion.js animations, fixed 08:00–01:00 axis, kept-day titles) and re-renders most calendar goldens, so you'll want to rebase after it merges. Reply here if you'd rather split it differently.

